#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:5 9f1bde10f82d408da0bd685b34be5a59
msgid "ARCHIVED: Analog Sonar (AC3.1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:7 bdc5cd8732b741708ce8f5b67dd0f55d
msgid "this document superceded by :ref:`common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:9 d68c01a3c4044eb2a20d8763d3600872
msgid ""
"Copter supports the MaxSonar line of sonar sensors for \"Terrain "
"Following\" while in Loiter or Alt Hold modes.  In these modes, the "
"copter will attempt to maintain a constant distance from the ground. The "
"sonar is also used during :ref:`LAND <land-mode>` mode.  The copter will "
"slow its descent to 50cm/s (configurable with LAND_SPEED parameter) when "
"the sonar detects something below the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:23 28099431ccc24524bb5f5faadc4751f7
msgid ""
"RNGFND_MAX_CM must be set to a tested, appropriate value.  If "
"RNGFND_MAX_CM is set to a value greater than the range of the sensor, the"
" autopilot will not respond correctly to the data provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:28 1ad1720479104a71ae5cd8c4f0eb5167
msgid "Supported Sonars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:30 d25ab134fbc240a49cdd847759e43413
msgid ""
"The Maxbotix recommended Sonar for Multicopter use is the `MaxBotix XL-"
"EZ4 <https://www.maxbotix.com/Ultrasonic_Sensors/MB1240.htm>`__ (aka "
"MB1240) which has a 7.65m max range and a narrow beam which helps reduce "
"the chance of interference from other sources of sound at the same "
"frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:34 38d841aeb33c4c72b1f7345f231c3d20
msgid ""
"It is definitely worth reading the `Interfacing an Ultrasonic Sensor with"
" a Pixhawk or ArduPilot Mega <https://www.maxbotix.com/articles"
"/ultrasonic-sensors-pixhawk-ardupilot.htm>`__ article by Maxbotix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:36 97906442738c487587631f26474bf9f8
msgid "These other sonar are also supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:38 ccd6faf064034e2fb64dc0dbda231be0
msgid ""
"`XL-EZL0 <https://www.maxbotix.com/Ultrasonic_Sensors/MB1260.htm>`__ "
"(10.68m max range but lower resolution, also XLL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:40 1e671165536b4bc18fbaa0060d8059d3
msgid ""
"`HRLV-EZ4 <https://www.sparkfun.com/products/11309>`__ (5m max range but "
"higher resolution, also HRLV-EZ0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:42 a59699236f05434db116bfab7c480449
msgid ""
"`LV-EZ4 <https://www.maxbotix.com/Ultrasonic_Sensors/MB1040.htm>`__ "
"(6.45m max range, cheaper but less resistant to noise, also LV_EZ0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:45 bf1844024b8a43eab71bbfa988e5a4d5
msgid "We do not yet support I2C based MaxBotix sonars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:48 b096054d77c04af4ad3fb5174de35947
msgid "Building a cable to reduce sonar noise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:50 68462ba9797d46548953263c53fa1239
msgid ""
"As described in `this Maxbotix article <https://www.maxbotix.com/articles"
"/maxsonar-troubleshooting.htm>`__, you will need to make a special cable "
"which requires:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:53 cfcd9e5f406b4b728a2124825245ff61
msgid "`100uF capacitor <https://www.sparkfun.com/products/96>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:54 e8186a6396bd42ff951ad2da3efcbc19
msgid "`10ohm resistor <https://www.sparkfun.com/products/10969>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:55 65aab67aa04f49a0b9799c62ed535acf
msgid "3-wire shielded cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:56 78e913d0f49a436eb604041817d68985
msgid ""
"`0.1\" crimp connector housing <https://www.pololu.com/product/1901>`__ "
"and `crimp pins <https://www.pololu.com/product/1930>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:62 b7e91a60e24347e1b9b92ca33b7a9a5e
msgid "Connecting the Sonar Sensor on APM 2.x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:64 9a559d0606d94770bd680e61eeda1b18
msgid ""
"The sensor's GND, V+ and \"AN\" or \"3\" pins should be connected to APM "
"2's A0 pins as shown in the diagram below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:71 84b86096f7b64ba48f19c0b0ab6829d5
msgid "Connecting the Sonar Sensor on PX4FMU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:73 6ceb28cac8a740f4a989ab3da9c09161
msgid ""
"You will need to assign the Sonar (signal line) to an appropriate PX4 pin"
" in Mission Planner - Configuration - Advanced Params - Adv Parameter "
"List using the SONAR_PIN parameter.  The following PX4 \"Pins\" are "
"available for SONAR use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:77 1298711cc2564a30b2c26fa9aa97c713
msgid "SONAR_PIN = 11 - (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:79 30a6a4d6bd2a424bbd4bdaa8f624bfe3
msgid ""
"The \"airspeed\" pin. Located on a 3 pin DF13 connector on the PX4IO "
"board, but directly visible to the ADC on the PX4FMU. This pin can take "
"voltages up to 6.6V (it has an internal voltage divider)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:82 56e181436d87411386d884f549496d7b
msgid "SONAR_PIN = 12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:84 4ca8fbb08c1444a981015f4bb35f82c7
msgid ""
"A general analog input pin. Located on pin 3 of the \"FMUSPI\" port on "
"the PX4IO board, this pin is directly visible to the PX4FMU analog input "
"code. This can take voltages up to 3.3V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:88 f5d93d68a5784defbdf89db3e380a1c4
msgid "SONAR_PIN = 13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:90 2b633a48854d4f53821da517783cbc06
msgid ""
"A general analog input pin. Located on pin 4 of the \"FMUSPI\" port on "
"the PX4IO board, this pin is directly visible to the PX4FMU analog input "
"code. This can take voltages up to 3.3V.  It is being worked on and will "
"be included in this section when it is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:96 d8c9701321b84a42bc6e31728e6b70c3
msgid "Mounting the Sonar Sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:98 9ee3fb564ba443a3a2f78fa98045d041
msgid ""
"It's important that the sonar sensor be mounted at least three inches "
"(10cm) away from sources of electrical noise including the ESCs and other"
" interference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:102 defb28d7a15b4d2fa0784643d5f0fa88
msgid "Enabling the Sonar through Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:104 ba55ad11b59f437c8a21582284708405
msgid ""
"Enable the sonar by connecting your APM/PX4 to the Mission Planner and "
"then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:106 042f59a2676843d49ca6b559c580d388
msgid "Go to Initial Setup > Optional Hardware > Sonar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:107 3429a05520e74ab5a2e8cf0a7a8befc9
msgid "Check the \"Enable\" checkbox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:108 2064185d4a284eb18210d23dfbf1678a
msgid "Select the sonar model from the drop down list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:114 29f08e6eb3eb4f3292c9bc3528da7c37
msgid "Testing the sonar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:116 cc2334062fd54721bba8c9528bdcb850
msgid ""
"You can test the sonar basically works by connecting your APM/PX4 to the "
"mission planner and then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:119 2920c046fc8a430d9ec19d7fd44eae9c
msgid ""
"Go to the Terminal window and press \"Connect to APM\" or \"Connect to "
"PX4\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:120 bac82cd5ec464c8cb31b2621cf441f69
msgid "when the prompt appears type *test*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:121 d68e8e1d761940b1b82c7ecacfa6839b
msgid "type *sonar*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:123 26ab35450dd54323b9123ab648378e99
msgid ""
"The current distanced sensed by the sonar should be displayed.  Aim the "
"sonar at targets of different distances (i.e. ceiling, wall, etc) and "
"ensure the numbers change.  If they do not then there may be a hardware "
"issue with the sonar or cabling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:128 1aaff21a8d7946f0a0a41e8330711eca
msgid ""
"You should also hear the sonar clicking very rapidly (10hz) whenever "
"power is applied if you do not hear this then it's possible that the "
"sonar is defective or is not being powered for some reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:133 994625b0339a4d88a6330878a67d9dca
msgid "Tuning the gain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:135 a16c6b64cf3049e1a389f5808048dd7c
msgid ""
"If when flying you find that your copter bobs up and down it is possible "
"that the default SONAR_GAIN is too high for your copter.  Go to the "
"mission planner's Config/Tuning > Full Parameter List and reduce the "
"SONAR_GAIN parameter from its default of 0.2 to 0.1 or even 0.05 and "
"press \"Write Params\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:142 2de95fb3230944dab163b445f682e077
msgid "Sonar Maximum Altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:144 40a4e80b65f14f85b214a85c18f589a2
msgid ""
"When enabled Sonar is used as the means of determining altitude below "
"Sonar Maximum Altitude, above that the barometer is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:146 281b312d7d374d6eb964002ce6b2586f
msgid ""
"Sonar Maximum Altitude is calculated as 60 percent of the factory "
"specified maximum Sonar range for the Sonar type selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:148 0cc4d57cb61a43a08ec7f35af576234d
msgid ""
"Sonar is used for determining altitude only when the Sonar itself is "
"detecting the ground and is below its Sonar Maximum Altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:151 25b7bce7894141c78d71504bf8bc0597
msgid ""
"XL-EZ4 or XL-EZ0 have a Maximum range of 7.65 meters and a Sonar Maximum "
"Altitude of 4.59 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:153 7a6abdee41e944bcb4793762ee29c8c7
msgid ""
"XL-EZLO have a Maximum range of 10.68 meters and a Sonar Maximum Altitude"
" = 6.4 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:155 1b18c830511b4ab4a420d67349390f9e
msgid ""
"HRLV-EZ4 or HRLV-EZ0 with Maximum range of 5 meters and a Sonar Maximum "
"Altitude of 3 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:157 47da4cd8d7ed457d960fe4fe6e34071d
msgid ""
"LV-EZ4 or LV-EZ0 have a Maximum range of 6.45 meters and a Sonar Maximum "
"Altitude = 3.87 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:160 d3e050d32500473d8451d9dc45cf0e11
msgid ""
"If the Sonar gets an unreliable return below the Sonar Maximum Altitude, "
"it is ignored and the Barometer altitude is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:164 4dd74d18558740f0aec083ffc87800fa
msgid "Cold weather performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:166 df5f16fd60c6403ba973e063f593f53b
msgid ""
"The :ref:`MaxBotix <common-rangefinder-maxbotix-analog>` XL-EZ0 sonar "
"(and other variations of their indoor sonar) may not function for about "
"10 minutes after an extreme drop in temperature (i.e. a drop from a warm "
"27C/80F house to the chilly 10C/50F outdoors) because of condensation "
"building up on the sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:172 bedba4f2d56a4dc2982b2a7668cf6421
msgid ""
"`This post "
"<https://diydrones.com/forum/topics/arducopter-2-0-48?xg_source=activity&id=705844%3ATopic%3A676942&page=31#comments>`__"
" includes one member's (`Geir Engebakken "
"<https://www.diydrones.com/forum/topic/listForContributor?user=3a28calx54gma>`__)"
" solution (initially suggested by the developer Olivier ADLER) involving "
"attaching 4x10Ohm resistors to the base of the sonar powered from a 5V "
"source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:179 866124f135354496b36583080ea4404c
msgid "Other Potential Causes of Sonar Noise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:181 002feb4cf55b441ebc6380905924756a
msgid ""
"If you are having problems with excessive noise on your sonar as shown in"
" the dataflash log below (sonar is in red, baro is in green)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:187 82957106c0d04c40a96b73c5e21919d6
msgid "There are a number of possible causes which should be investigated:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:189 0766d201bc7146dbb22d0f15461e496b
msgid ""
"Sonar is susceptible to \"noise\" from a variety of sources and several "
"\"fixes\" may be required to achieve adequate performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:192 660d4ef2f29c43e9b9e5ac612643eeb2
msgid ""
"Electrical noise caused by ESCs, Servos, or switching BEC's on the same "
"circuit as the Sonar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:195 65deda2519134e3ea0b16c0e1d726522
msgid ""
"The RC filter and use of shielded cable as described above are usually "
"sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:198 d83af3dff65846ac99231adb206cd9a4
msgid "EMF radiation from motors, motor wires, ESC's or Xbee."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:200 2d9b65e0bad1434f8e8c581fbafce3f8
msgid ""
"Sonar is especially susceptible to AC EMF noise generated by the ESCs and"
" ESC to motor wiring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:202 34677db718ef42f1b57d14cc42a35266
msgid ""
"This can be greatly reduced by wrapping the nearby ESCs and their motor "
"wiring in aluminum (gutter) tape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:205 936682d3385e4e469657e09ff901c67d
msgid "Acoustic noise from propellers, prop wash and turbulence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:207 5a3f1151f41f44eca249aafc16c28546
msgid ""
"It is very important to keep the Sonar out of direct prop wash or "
"turbulence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:209 853ed37b004b44c597ef8607ea3cfaeb
msgid "Balancing propellers (and motors) can help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:210 153dbf8d7b4345a89078a936ccb5f46e
msgid ""
"Mounting the sonar sensor inside a small can or tube thinly lined with "
"foam can greatly reduce unwanted exterior acoustic noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:212 62dafce34b4444f59f725d5ad0d35226
msgid ""
"Wrap Sonar module board and components in rubber or foam tape to reduce "
"transferred acoustic noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:215 bd8c6edb740e43cdb4deded031b423f0
msgid "Vibration from motors, props, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:217 078ec9fc93de451ea3d5b7b4f7d0832d
msgid "Sonar is very subject to frame transmitted vibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:218 0ac40bd364814b90b64df0f92e4921ef
msgid ""
"Mounting the Sonar module on double sided foam or Gel tape will pretty "
"much eliminate this noise source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:221 9b48a5a5cc7e47bcb9dfa9aabd3ab9eb
msgid ""
"The MB 1240 series is the only Sonar considered suitable for multicopter "
"use by the manufacturer - Maxbotix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sonar.rst:226 610ae8f0ee224412b28a68812544c9aa
msgid ""
"Please read this tutorial for a comprehensive review: `Interfacing an "
"Ultrasonic Sensor with a Pixhawk or ArduPilot Mega "
"<https://www.maxbotix.com/articles/ultrasonic-sensors-pixhawk-"
"ardupilot.htm>`__."
msgstr ""

